# Who must approve what.
#
# This file is inert on its own. It becomes enforcement only when branch
# protection on `main` requires a review from Code Owners — until then it
# documents an intention and stops nothing. See docs/ROADMAP.md 3.1 and 7.3.
#
# Why it exists alongside `agents scope`: the two catch the same mistake at
# different moments and neither substitutes for the other. `agents scope`
# tells a contributor immediately, in their own session and in CI, that their
# branch strayed — fast, specific, and skippable by anyone who simply does not
# run it. This file is checked by GitHub at merge, so it is not skippable at
# all. Fast feedback, then a lock.

# Everything, by default. A file nobody thought to name below still needs an
# owner, and the owner is the maintainer.
*                       @siddak1234

# The platform. Depended on by every agent, so a change here is a change to
# all of them.
/orchestrator/          @siddak1234
/registry.yaml          @siddak1234
/pyproject.toml         @siddak1234
/uv.lock                @siddak1234

# The contract other people implement.
/docs/AGENT_PROTOCOL.md @siddak1234

# CI, and the review board itself.
#
# `.claude/` is named explicitly rather than left to the `*` rule above, and
# the reason is concrete. A branch that rewrote `.claude/agents/` — the four
# reviewers — used to pass `agents scope` clean whenever it touched no agent
# folder, and CI would then have run those rewritten reviewers against the very
# diff that rewrote them. `agents scope` now refuses that branch; this line is
# the half that cannot be bypassed by not running a command.
/.github/               @siddak1234
/.claude/               @siddak1234
/.pre-commit-config.yaml @siddak1234
/.gitignore             @siddak1234
/.gitattributes         @siddak1234

# Agents are their author's, reviewed by the maintainer. Add a line per agent
# as contributors arrive — `/agents/parcel-geo/ @siddak1234 @their-handle` —
# so review routes to someone who knows the code.
/agents/                @siddak1234
